## 🧪 Methodology

```
Raw Dataset
    │
    ▼
Data Preprocessing
    ├── Label Encoding (Gender, Lung Cancer)
    ├── ADASYN Oversampling (class balancing)
    └── Feature Scaling
    │
    ▼
Train/Test Split (75/25)
    │
    ▼
10 ML Models Trained & Evaluated
    │
    ▼
Performance Comparison (AUC, Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F-Measure)
```

### Models Evaluated

| # | Model | Description |
|---|-------|-------------|
| 1 | **Logistic Regression** | Statistical binary classifier |
| 2 | **Decision Tree** | Recursive feature-based partitioning |
| 3 | **K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)** | Instance-based lazy learner |
| 4 | **Gaussian Naive Bayes** | Probabilistic classifier (continuous features) |
| 5 | **Multinomial Naive Bayes** | Probabilistic classifier (frequency vectors) |
| 6 | **Support Vector Classifier (SVC)** | Hyperplane-based maximum margin classifier |
| 7 | **Random Forest** | Ensemble of decision trees with bagging |
| 8 | **XGBoost** | Optimized gradient boosting |
| 9 | **Multilayer Perceptron (MLP)** | Feedforward artificial neural network |
| 10 | **Gradient Boosting** | Sequential ensemble of weak learners |

### Preprocessing Steps

- **Label Encoding** — Categorical variables (`Gender`, `Lung Cancer`) converted to numeric using scikit-learn's `LabelEncoder`
- **ADASYN Oversampling** — Adaptive Synthetic Sampling to handle class imbalance
- **Feature Scaling** — Standardization for models sensitive to feature magnitude
- **PCA** — Principal Component Analysis for dimensionality reduction

