## 📝 Key Findings

- **Random Forest** outperformed all other models with an AUC of 0.9919, confirming its strength for ensemble classification on tabular health data
- **XGBoost** and **Gradient Boosting** were close runners-up, both achieving 97.60% accuracy
- **ADASYN oversampling** effectively addressed the class imbalance, improving model recall across all classifiers
- Lifestyle factors (smoking, alcohol consumption) and clinical symptoms (coughing, shortness of breath, chest pain) were among the most predictive features
- Even without overt disease symptoms, ML-based risk-factor monitoring can support early screening and clinical follow-up

